--TEST--
A PHP-style `function (…) { … }` anonymous function passed to a generic Core call reports its own refusal and nothing else: neither the argument nor the call's inferred result type reports a mismatch — `rule:types/anonymous-function`
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<int> $prices = [1, 2];
array<string> $labels = Core\Arr::map($prices, function(int $n): string { return 'n' . $n; });
echo Core\Str::join($labels, ', '), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0222]: anonymous `function` expressions are not supported
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
